The vendor branch is vendor/ncurses/dist, tagged
vendor/ncurses/dist/X.Y.  It holds pristine upstream sources trimmed with
MIDNIGHTBSD-Xlist; the local changes (see below) live only on master.
The 6.3 and 6.4 commits on the vendor branch are untrimmed and were
never merged; 6.6 is the first import after 6.2 to reach master.

To import a new release:

  1) Fetch ncurses-X.Y.tar.gz and its .asc and verify the signature.
  2) On a checkout of vendor/ncurses/dist:
	git rm -rq .
	tar -X MIDNIGHTBSD-Xlist -xzf ncurses-X.Y.tar.gz
	cp -Rp ncurses-X.Y/ ./ && rm -rf ncurses-X.Y
	git add -A && git commit && git tag -a vendor/ncurses/dist/X.Y
  3) On master:
	git merge -X subtree=contrib/ncurses vendor/ncurses/dist
  4) Update the glue in lib/ncurses:
     - ncurses/ncurses_cfg.h: bump NCURSES_VERSION_STRING and compare
       against include/ncurses_defs for new or renamed HAVE_* and USE_*
       macros.  Keep USE_ROOT_ENVIRON, USE_SETUID_ENVIRON and
       USE_ROOT_ACCESS undefined, and HAVE_GETUID defined: since 6.5 the
       root/setuid environment checks in tinfo/access.c are compiled out
       entirely when HAVE_GETUID is missing.
     - ncurses/Makefile: every @VAR@ in include/curses.h.in,
       include/MKterm.h.awk.in, termcap.h.in, unctrl.h.in and
       ncurses_dll.h.in must have a sed rule in the matching target.
       Check the generated curses.h and term.h for leftover @...@.
     - Compare the module lists (ncurses/modules etc.) with SRCS.
     - ncurses/termcap.c is our own termcap reader, used instead of
       tinfo/read_termcap.c; check it still builds against changed
       internals (6.6 made _nc_delink_entry static).
     FreeBSD's lib/ncurses (split into tinfo/ and ncurses/) is a useful
     reference for Makefile and ncurses_cfg.h changes.
  5) Build lib/ncurses/{ncurses,form,menu,panel}, compare
     nm -D --defined-only against the installed libraries (SHLIB_MAJOR
     stays at 9 while upstream keeps ABI 6), and note the update in
     UPDATING.

Local changes carried on master relative to the vendor branch:

  ncurses/base/lib_mouse.c     - include <sys/consio.h> for sysmouse
                                 support on MidnightBSD.
  ncurses/tinfo/lib_baudrate.c - include <sys/param.h> and use the
                                 NCURSES_OSPEED_COMPAT speed table on
                                 MidnightBSD.

The cc also defines __FreeBSD__, so both are belt and braces.  The
CVE-2021-39537 (captoinfo.c), CVE-2025-6141 (parse_entry.c) and
infocmp.c initializer-size fixes we used to carry were adopted upstream
by 6.6.
